<https://repolex.ai/data/jmespath/jmespath.py/blob/a352d69eb42c67f9630eb4ecdd952c7ef792af34#test_can_max_datetimes> <https://repolex.ai/ontology/extracts/tree-sitter/tree-sitter/v0.25/core/text> "def test_can_max_datetimes(self):\n        # This is python specific behavior, but JMESPath does not specify what\n        # you should do with language specific types.  We're going to add the\n        # ability that ``to_string`` will always default to str()'ing values it\n        # doesn't understand.\n        data = [datetime.now(), datetime.now() + timedelta(seconds=1)]\n        result = jmespath.search('max([*].to_string(@))', data)\n        self.assertEqual(json.loads(result), str(data[-1]))" <https://repolex.ai/data/jmespath/jmespath.py/blob/a352d69eb42c67f9630eb4ecdd952c7ef792af34> .
